ssion":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"regression","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase-1 RCA (confirmed before repair): Gerrit Verified run 31726058931 failed identically in all four matrix cells before pytest. The runtime gate reported `src/rebar/_config_schema.py` at 808 LOC against the locked 800-LOC cap. The triggering main commit d2dea317ec added eight schema lines after prior work had exhausted headroom; change 1730's importer code never ran. A direct RED oracle in the fresh worktree reproduces `assert 808 <= 800`. The changeable artifact is the inline `_SECTIONS` registry at `src/rebar/_config_schema.py:605-742`, an existing independent seam that can move without changing its 97-key coercion contract. Alternative causes (importer behavior, platform/Python version, pytest) are ruled out by the pre-test, cross-platform identical failure. Defect legitimacy: this violates the locked module-size contract in `tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py` and AGENTS.md. Expected repair behavior: the schema module is below 800 LOC while every registry key/coercer remains observable through the existing import paths.","timestamp":1786643721554613001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Final rebar-debug report. Problem: every Gerrit Verified change failed before pytest because merged main exceeded the locked module-size cap. Proven root cause: d2dea317ec added eight config-schema lines after headroom was exhausted, leaving src/rebar/_config_schema.py at 808 LOC; runs 31726058931 and 31730396829 reproduced the identical failure across all four OS/Python cells, ruling out the importer patch, pytest, and platform variance. Test: held-out /tmp/rebar_config_sections_oracle.py was RED at 808 > 800 before repair, GREEN after repair, RED again when one registry entry was removed (96 != 97), then restored GREEN; it also exercised representative coercions. Fix: commit ea6ee67e6a/change 1732 extracted the unchanged 14-section/97-key _SECTIONS registry to a 146-line leaf and reduced _config_schema.py to 677 lines. Safety: public import/re-export paths remain intact, no caller depends on registry colocation, no capability/dependency/default/test changed, and no existing assertion was weakened. Siblings: no same-file instance remains; the broader repo-wide size sweep cinderlike-lucky-akitainu remains deliberately deferred and was not consumed. Residual advisory: the schema module docstring's old 'stdlib-only' wording already contradicted pre-existing rebar._config_coercion/_deprecations imports; accepted as unrelated documentation debt rather than restart the main-outage gate. Replication: lint/typecheck passed, 54 focused tests passed, the exact macOS-shaped lane passed 12,840 tests/52 skips locally, and Gerrit run 31730781652 passed all jobs with LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, and zero unresolved comments before merge.","timestamp":1786647691023302001}],"created_at":1786643335315066001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"5d3da993-6b8b-471f-8d26-151d963e706c","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"325e-7e85-d0d6-4318"},{"link_uuid":"b351e1b9-4bbd-40f8-bbb2-3c31b996686e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"69d2-0ec0-9ef0-4ecd"}],"description":"## Context and confirmed defect\n\nMerged main at d2dea317ec fails every Gerrit Verified matrix cell before pytest: `src/rebar/_config_schema.py` is 808 LOC against the locked 800-LOC cap. Change 1730 reproduced the same failure on Ubuntu Python 3.11/3.12/3.13 and macOS Python 3.13 in run 31726058931. The importer patch never executed. This is distinct from deferred repo-wide sweep cinderlike-lucky-akitainu: it is the narrow main-is-red regression blocking all changes.\n\n## Root cause\n\nTwo individually reviewed config additions accumulated through Gerrit's server-side main history without preserving module-size headroom. The monolithic `_SECTIONS` coercion registry remains colocated with dataclasses despite already being an import-independent table over `_config_coercion` helpers, leaving the schema module above its enforced hard cap.\n\n## Plan\n\n- Extract the complete `_SECTIONS` registry, unchanged, to a new `src/rebar/_config_sections.py` leaf that imports only the coercion helpers it calls.\n- Import `_SECTIONS` back into `_config_schema.py`; preserve every key, coercer, validation bound, and public behavior.\n- Prove structural equivalence with the config tests and full lint/typecheck gates; seed a mutation that removes one registry entry and confirm existing config-surface coverage catches it.\n- Do not raise or alter the 800-LOC limit and do not broaden into the deferred repo-wide sweep.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `src/rebar/_config_schema.py` is below 800 LOC and the new module is at least 100 LOC, following the existing registry seam.\n- [x] Every `_SECTIONS` section/key and coercer is preserved exactly; config-surface and focused config tests pass.\n- [x] The module-size gate, lint, and typecheck pass.\n- [x] A defect-seeded missing-registry-entry mutation is observed RED, then the final implementation is restored GREEN.\n\n## File impact\n\n- `src/rebar/_config_schema.py` — replace the inline coercion registry with an import.\n- `src/rebar/_config_sections.py` — hold the unchanged coercion registry in its independent leaf module.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_config_schema.py","reason":"Replace the inline coercion registry with an import while preserving schema behavior."},{"path":"src/rebar/_config_sections.py","reason":"New leaf module containing the unchanged section-to-coercer registry."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","69d2-0ec0-9ef0-4ecd"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"7058a7b7-9d6d-4dc3-be0e-6608b71f14dc","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["ci","module-size","regression"],"ticket_id":"9843-170c-4d9e-446b","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Restore main CI after _config_schema.py exceeded the locked module-size cap","verify_commands":[{"command":"pytest tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py -q","dd_id":"AC1","dd_text":"Schema and extracted module satisfy the module-size policy."},{"command":"pytest tests/unit/test_config_typed.py tests/unit/test_config_surface_golden.py -q","dd_id":"AC2","dd_text":"Config schema and public surface remain behaviorally unchanged."},{"command":"make lint && make typecheck","dd_id":"AC3","dd_text":"Static quality gates pass."}]},"source_event_uuids":["fdb53b86-ad25-49b7-8d04-2b18fb505712","1c929f0a-231d-4658-895f-a680a0082a85","f7756fe2-40a4-4b2f-8af0-7581b09834e1","b2c5f399-9f1f-4380-a3b0-f3925fb03d89","e27f92a6-dbdf-486a-a398-f41a25ae3938","14a6a1dd-4344-4a3b-9f9d-3b2faeeaa8d9","a86da74b-60a4-42a0-8653-09ee540c1e07","6bb39874-3d45-4cad-a824-6c4b3a0e142c","47bbc4b6-76b8-4bf7-82ad-3f150b5a5ec9","ffbf34fa-2218-4083-a41f-cfbe2499b1f6","5d3da993-6b8b-471f-8d26-151d963e706c","b351e1b9-4bbd-40f8-bbb2-3c31b996686e","3637de0f-e762-49b8-afa0-0807581b7306","076b6231-8437-4973-8b89-115d86a15701","7058a7b7-9d6d-4dc3-be0e-6608b71f14dc","0a63c551-5fe4-43c6-b522-fc95b6aaeb08"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786659636008156001,"uuid":"5257dad1-6c8d-484d-a73d-d579513ce9c5"}